{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/how-qr-codes-work/audio/main-47901e8ded05.mp3","durationSec":122.568,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.56,"text":"A QR code is a two-dimensional pattern of black and white squares."},{"start":4.44,"end":6.98,"text":"The letters QR stand for Quick Response."},{"start":7.7,"end":16.7,"text":"Unlike a barcode, which only stores information in one direction (left to right), a QR code stores information in two directions — across and down."},{"start":17.42,"end":20.1,"text":"This means it can hold much more data in a small space."},{"start":20.76,"end":26.86,"text":"For example, a single QR code can store a full website address, a phone number, or even a short message."},{"start":27.38,"end":31.54,"text":"The small black and white squares inside a QR code are called modules."},{"start":32.68,"end":36.44,"text":"Every module is either black or white, and together they form a code."},{"start":37.1,"end":43.5,"text":"A simple QR code — for example, one that stores just a short word — needs fewer modules and is smaller."},{"start":44.32,"end":50.62,"text":"A complex QR code — for example, one that stores a long web address — needs more modules and becomes larger."},{"start":51.24,"end":53.9,"text":"The more data you put in, the bigger the code gets."},{"start":54.28,"end":58.36,"text":"Look at a QR code and you will notice three square shapes in three corners."},{"start":59,"end":60.38,"text":"These are called position patterns."},{"start":60.82,"end":67.44,"text":"They help your phone's camera find the code and understand which direction it is facing — even if the code is upside down or tilted."},{"start":68.24,"end":74.6,"text":"Once the camera locates the three corner squares, it reads the modules across and down and turns the pattern into data."},{"start":75.24,"end":78.78,"text":"This is why scanning is so fast: the position patterns act like a map."},{"start":79.44,"end":82.86,"text":"A QR code has a built-in safety feature called error correction."},{"start":83.44,"end":90.9,"text":"This means that even if part of the code is dirty, torn, or covered, some missing data can still be restored and read correctly."},{"start":91.72,"end":96.14,"text":"The code stores extra information that helps rebuild some missing pieces automatically."},{"start":96.88,"end":100.24,"text":"This is why a QR code may still work when a small part is hard to see."},{"start":100.62,"end":104.44,"text":"QR codes are useful, but they can also open harmful or fake websites."},{"start":105.62,"end":110.34,"text":"Scammers may use a QR code to send you to a page that tries to steal your personal information."},{"start":111.52,"end":115.04,"text":"Before you open a link, always check the web address on your screen."},{"start":115.86,"end":122.24,"text":"If the address looks strange, the code is unexpected, or it pressures you to act quickly, do not open it."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"QR","start":0.18,"end":0.48},{"text":"code","start":0.48,"end":0.78},{"text":"is","start":0.78,"end":0.98},{"text":"a","start":0.98,"end":1.12},{"text":"two-dimensional","start":1.12,"end":1.78},{"text":"pattern","start":1.78,"end":2.24},{"text":"of","start":2.24,"end":2.5},{"text":"black","start":2.5,"end":2.76},{"text":"and","start":2.76,"end":2.94},{"text":"white","start":2.94,"end":3.16},{"text":"squares","start":3.16,"end":3.56},{"text":"The","start":4.44,"end":4.56},{"text":"letters","start":4.56,"end":4.86},{"text":"QR","start":4.86,"end":5.28},{"text":"stand","start":5.28,"end":5.9},{"text":"for","start":5.9,"end":6.16},{"text":"Quick","start":6.16,"end":6.42},{"text":"Response","start":6.42,"end":6.98},{"text":"Unlike","start":7.7,"end":7.98},{"text":"a","start":7.98,"end":8.14},{"text":"barcode","start":8.14,"end":8.66},{"text":"which","start":8.8,"end":8.92},{"text":"only","start":8.92,"end":9.3},{"text":"stores","start":9.3,"end":9.66},{"text":"information","start":9.66,